===Etymology===
{{inh+|fr|frm|espaule}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|espalle}}, from {{inh|fr|VL.||*spatla}},<ref>Clédat, Léon. 1905. Revue de philologie française et de littérature, tome XIX. Paris: Librairie Émile Bouillon. Page 71. https://books.google.com/books?id=SdsxAAAAMAAJ&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false</ref> from {{inh|fr|LL.|spatula|spathula|flat, broad piece}},<ref>{{R:fr:TLFi|épaule|etym=1}}</ref> diminutive of {{inh|fr|la|spatha||straight sword}} (whence French {{m|fr|épée||sword}}). {{doublet|fr|spatule}}, which was a borrowing.

